course: dictionary
lesson: 4404
title: Half: one of two equal parts
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: Half is a small word with several jobs. As a noun, a half is one of two equal parts of something. «A half of 12 is 6.» Split 12 into two equal piles and each pile is a half.
explain: As an adjective, half comes before a noun and describes an amount: «half an hour» is 30 minutes, and «half past 3» is 3:30. As an adverb, half means partly, as in «half asleep». You are not fully asleep, only part of the way there.
explain: Look at the words around half to work out which job it does. Is it a part of something, a length of time, or a feeling like being partly awake? The clues are in the sentence, just as with any other context word.
fact: A half is one of two equal parts of something.
fact: «Half» can be a noun, an adjective, or an adverb, so check the words around it.
fact: «Half past 3» means 30 minutes after 3 o'clock, which is 3:30.
fact: «Half an hour» means 30 minutes.
fact: «Half» can mean partly, as in «half asleep». A third of 12 is 4, and a fourth of 12 is 3, so a half is always the biggest of these parts.
exercise: «A half of 12 is 6.» What is a half of 12? | 3 | *6 | 4 | 8
exercise: «The train leaves at half past 3.» What time does the train leave? | *3:30 | 3:15 | 4:30 | 3:00
exercise: Mum says, «I'll be back in half an hour.» How long will she be? | 45 minutes | 60 minutes | 15 minutes | *30 minutes
test: In «She was half asleep on the sofa», what does half mean? | Completely | *Partly | Twice | Never
test: Which phrase means 30 minutes after the hour? | *half past | half of | half asleep | half-time
exam: Which word means one of two equal parts of something? | Whole | Quarter | Halves | *Half
